Bare AND/OR/NOT in operator position are not SSL operators
(diag.bare_logical_operator, error, on the bare word). A bare word before
a parenthesis is still the operator, so it is not also a
direct_procedure_call, and the operand after a prefix Not is not also an
unexpected_token (issue #255): one finding per typo.
Suspected issue: under strict, undeclared_variable also reports 'AND' (line 3) and 'Not' (line 9) — the catalog says the sibling rules defer so "one typo is one finding" (issue #255); 'or (' and the later 'NOT (' are not reported, so the extra finding is also inconsistent.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE CanRelease;
	:PARAMETERS bApproved, bPaid, bOnHold;
	:IF bApproved AND bPaid;
		:RETURN .T.;
	:ENDIF;
	:IF bApproved or (bPaid);
		:RETURN .T.;
	:ENDIF;
	:IF Not bOnHold;
		:RETURN .T.;
	:ENDIF;
	:RETURN NOT (bOnHold);
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE CanRelease;
	:PARAMETERS bApproved, bPaid, bOnHold;
	:IF bApproved AND bPaid;
		:RETURN .T.;
	:ENDIF;

	:IF bApproved or(bPaid);
		:RETURN .T.;
	:ENDIF;

	:IF Not bOnHold;
		:RETURN .T.;
	:ENDIF;
	:RETURN NOT(bOnHold);
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
3:16-3:19 error bare_logical_operator: Use '.AND.' instead of 'AND' for logical operations in SSL
6:16-6:18 error bare_logical_operator: Use '.OR.' instead of 'or' for logical operations in SSL
9:6-9:9 error bare_logical_operator: Use '.NOT.' instead of 'Not' for logical operations in SSL
12:10-12:13 error bare_logical_operator: Use '.NOT.' instead of 'NOT' for logical operations in SSL
